-- title:
--   Diamond times Frobenius determinant equals ℓ on Tₚ J_H
-- statement:
--   Fix a natural number $M \neq 0$, a prime $p$, a subgroup $H \le (\mathbb{Z}/M)^{\times}$ and a finite set $S$ of natural numbers, and assume [`ModularCurve.HeckeDiamondInputsHAll M H`](def/ModularCurve_XHOperators.html#L113): for every prime $\ell$ the named inputs for the Hecke correspondence along $\ell$ on the function field of $X_H(M)$ base changed to $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ (a defined $\beta$, integrality of $\alpha$ and $\beta$, existence of principal divisors, finiteness, the fundamental identity and the norm formula) hold, and for every $d \in (\mathbb{Z}/M)^{\times}$ there is an automorphism of that field over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ realising the diamond operator $\langle d\rangle$. Let $V = \mathbb{Q}_p \otimes_{\mathbb{Z}_p} T_p(J_H(M))$, where $J_H(M)$ is the group of degree-zero divisor classes of the base-changed function field and $T_p$ is the group of sequences $(x_n)$ with $p^n x_n = 0$ and $p\,x_{n+1} = x_n$, and let $R \subseteq \operatorname{End}_{\mathbb{Q}_p}(V)$ be the $\mathbb{Q}_p$-subalgebra generated by the base changes of the operators $T_\ell$, $U_q$, $\langle d\rangle$ attached to the generators [`CohCarrier.Gen M S`](def/CohCarrier_Inst.html#L13). Let $b = (b_0, b_1)$ be a basis of $V$ as an $R$-module indexed by `Fin 2`. Let $\ell$ be a prime with $\ell \notin S$, $\ell \nmid M$ and $\ell \neq p$, let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with $\ell$ a nonunit of $A$, and let $\sigma$ be a $\mathbb{Q}$-algebra automorphism of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ lying in the decomposition subgroup of $A$ over $\mathbb{Q}$ and acting on the residue field of $A$ by $x \mapsto x^{\ell}$. Writing $a_{ij} \in R$ for the coordinates of the image of $b_i$ under the base change to $\mathbb{Q}_p$ of the Galois action of $\sigma$ on $T_p(J_H(M))$, the conclusion is the identity in $\operatorname{End}_{\mathbb{Q}_p}(V)$ $$\langle \ell \rangle \cdot (a_{00}a_{11} - a_{10}a_{01}) = \ell,$$ where $\langle \ell \rangle$ is the diamond operator at the unit class of $\ell$ in $(\mathbb{Z}/M)^{\times}$ and $\ell$ on the right denotes $\ell$ times the identity.
--
--   This is the Weil-pairing determinant relation for the Galois representation on the rational $p$-adic Tate module of $J_H(M)$: the determinant of a Frobenius element at $\ell$, computed in any basis over the Hecke–diamond algebra, equals $\langle \ell \rangle^{-1}\ell$. It feeds the computation of the trace and determinant of Frobenius on the relevant rank-two piece and the construction of the rational rank-two nebentypus family.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_diamond_mul_coordDet_eq_of_basis_rationalTateModule_jH.lean

